<title>SWEDEN: Celsius proposes '96 dividend of 3.40 Skr.</title>
<headline>Celsius proposes '96 dividend of 3.40 Skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish defence group Celsius AB reported its final 1996 earnings on Thursday.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Proposed dividend/share (crowns)     3.40 vs nil</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    347 vs    559 LOSS</p>
<p> Sales					11,112 vs 10,817</p>
<p> Order intake			     10,455 vs  9,055</p>
<p> Operating costs			  10,771 vs 11,181</p>
<p> Depreciation				  480 vs    631</p>
<p> Associate interest		 CREDIT  21 vs     47 CHARGE</p>
<p> Operating result after deprec  PROFIT  99 vs    793 LOSS</p>
<p> Net financial items			 248 vs    234</p>
<p> Minorities				    nil vs	2 CHARGE</p>
<p> Pre-tax result		   PROFIT   347 vs    561 LOSS</p>
<p> Tax						62 vs     36</p>
<p> Net result			 PROFIT   285 vs    597 LOSS</p>
<p>NOTE -- The company released preliminary 1996 earnings on February 10, saying its profit after financial items amounted to 347 million crowns and sales to more than 11 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
